    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x3020/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x3020/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x3020/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x3020 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reinstall the add-in card. If the issue persists, update the card's firmware.
Update firmware
1.  Go to https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home.
2.  Under Documentation and Software, click Knowledge Base.
3.  Enter System ROM 2.20 in the search bar, and then click search.
4.  Click Drivers and Software.
5.  Under Operating System, select the correct operating system.
6.  Under Software Type, select BIOS (Entitlement Required).
7.  Under Software Subtype, select System ROM.
8.  Select the appropriate patch, and then click Download.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/
public/home, and then click Check Status under Warranty.
This enables Hewlett Packard Enterprise to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure
has been confirmed. For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product
maintenance and service guide.
2.  Create a support case at http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
