  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0393/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0393 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">For more information on sanitizing NVDIMMs, see the HPE 16GB NVDIMM User Guide on the Hewlett
Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/info/NVDIMM-docs).
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can damage the DIMM components and the system board
connector. For more information, see the DIMM handling guidelines in the troubleshooting guide for your
product on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website:
•  HPE ProLiant Gen10 (http://www.hpe.com/info/gen10-troubleshooting)
•  HPE Synergy (http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-troubleshootings)
If this issue persists create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Warranty Status.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0393/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0393/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0393/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0393/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0393/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
