    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0013-0x0021/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0013-0x0021/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0013-0x0021/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  Allow sufficient time for the rebuild to complete.
2.  Verify that all cables are properly connected.
3.  To replace the failed drive:
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Check Status under the Warranty
Check heading.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed.
For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance
and service guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.
4.  After you receive the replacement drives. Remove all power.
1.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
2.  Disconnect each power cord from the server.
5.  Replace the drive if it has failed.
6.  Replace the drive if missing.
7.  Replace the incorrect drive.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0021 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Cable%20or%20connector"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0013-0x0021/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
