  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1719/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1719/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1719/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1719/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1719/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x1719 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Do the following:
Option 1: Update the controller to the latest firmware version.
Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more
information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an
accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each
of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are
available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation).
To update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide
and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses
Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components.
To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and
Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.
Option 2: Create an HPE Support Case and replace the controller..
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1010">
    <diag:severity rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAJOR</diag:severity>
    <diag:concernsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
    <diag:concernsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Storage%20drive"/>
    <diag:sourcePage rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">211</diag:sourcePage>
    <diag:sourcePage rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">212</diag:sourcePage>
    <diag:recordId rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1010</diag:recordId>
    <diag:eventName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">fltStorageVirtualDriveConsistencyCheckFailed</diag:eventName>
    <diag:similarTo rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1008"/>
    <diag:similarTo rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1009"/>
    <diag:similarTo rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1007"/>
    <diag:recommendsProcedure rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1010/procedure/01"/>
    <diag:explanation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">NOTE: This fault is not currently implemented by UCSMThis fault is present only as a placeholder, possibly for another release,such as stand-alone rack servers.--- This fault occurs when a drive consistency check operation has failed. This may cause a degradation in performance.</diag:explanation>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/unified_computing/ucs/ucs-manager/Reference-Docs/Faults-Error-Msgs/6-0/b_cisco_ucs_faults_and_error_messages_reference-6-0.pdf"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#EventDefinition"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:vendor rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Cisco</diag:vendor>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cisco F1010: fltStorageVirtualDriveConsistencyCheckFailed</rdfs:label>
