  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0233/procedure/01">
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/System%20board"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Re-seat the DIMMs in the identified channel and update the System ROM. Inspect DIMM sockets and the
system board for bent pins or damaged traces.
Perform the following procedure for each affected DIMM.
1.  At the next available maintenance window power down your server.
2.  Remove all power.
a.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
b.  Disconnect each power cord from the server.
3.  Remove the DIMM.
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system
board connector. See the DIMM handling guidelines on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Library at:
http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs
4.  Clean the DIMM and the DIMM slot with anti-static compressed air.
5.  Reinstall the DIMM.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0233/procedure/01/item/009"/>
