  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N34f4a2cb97c24522836ff30f0a555b0a">
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-DIAG0151"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-DIAG0151/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: SMART Predictive Failure indicates the hard drive has failed SMART and maybe nearing the end of its life. Other types of &lt;Error Reason&gt; in this category may indicate an intermittent or firmware problem, rerun the test again. Desktops, servers: Check the hard disk drive cables and connections. All systems: If error persists, make sure that hard disk drive firmware and BIOS are current. The &lt;80000000000000??&gt; value is an EFI error code returned by the driver.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Storage%20drive"/>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-DIAG0151/procedure/01"/>
  </rdf:Description>
