  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0521/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0521/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0521/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0521/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0521/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0521/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0521 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0521/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the unsupported backplane and install the drive backplane in a supported configuration. Consult
documentation for configuration guidelines.
For more information, see the server maintenance and service guide for your product on the Hewlett
Packard Enterprise website:
•  HPE ProLiant Gen10 (http://www.hpe.com/info/proliantgen10-docs)
•  HPE Synergy (http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs)
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Warranty Status.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-CUPD4130/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1) Review the health audit details in the console update logs for the specific failing check.2. Disk
space: Free up space on the appliance or add more disk space.3. CPU/Memory: Wait for high-load
operations to complete, or increase resources if virtualized.4. Retry the upgrade after resolving the
health issue.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dell CUPD4130 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-CUPD4130/procedure/01/item/001"/>
  </rdf:Description>
