    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0365/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0365/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0365/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0365/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0365 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0365/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove and replace the unsupported NVDIMM-Ns with compatible NVDIMM-Ns.
1.  Remove all power.
a.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
b.  Disconnect each power cord from the server
2.  Remove the DIMM.
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system
board connector. See the DIMM handling guidelines on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Library at:
http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs
3.  Install the new DIMM.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
