  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0277/procedure/01/item/001">
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If you see this fault, Corrective action maybe taken based on reason information in the fault description whenever such a reason is displayed. If the fault description displays reason as "ENM source pinning failed" then it means that the fabric interconnect is operating in End-host Node Mode and the uplink port that this server facing port is pinned to is down or does not have appropriate VLAN configured. In case of such an error for an appliance port check the VLAN configuration on uplink port. A VLAN with same id as the one on the appliance port will also need to be configured on the uplink port. After setting the configuration right if you still see the fault then create a show tech-support file for Cisco UCS Manager and the chassis or FEX module, and then contact Cisco TAC.</diag:itemText>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">1</diag:itemOrder>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 788); UNNUMBERED_SOURCE_BLOCK; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: NO_DOCUMENTED_CAUSE. No documented cause in this source solution group; do not invent a cause.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cisco F0277 printed item 1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
