    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Verify the logical drive configuration using HPE SSA.
For more information, see the HPE Smart Storage Administrator User Guide on the Hewlett Packard
Enterprise website (https://www.hpe.com/info/smartstorage-docs).</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0318/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0318/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0318/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0318/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0318/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0318/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0318/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0318/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0318 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0318/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  When a TPM is installed and is being used with BitLocker, be sure the TPM is enabled in UEFI System
Utilities. See the UEFI System Utilities user guide for your product, and see the TPM replacement
recovery procedure in the operating system documentation.
2.  When a TPM is installed, be sure that the TPM is configured for a mode that is compatible with the OS
running on the server. Verify that the OS supports the version of TPM installed and configured on the
server.
3.  When a TPM 2.0 is installed, verify that the server is configured for UEFI boot mode.
4.  Leave the TPM installed, and request a new system board and TPM from a Hewlett Packard
Enterprise authorized service provider.
a.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to https://support.hpe.com/
hpesc/public/home, and then click Warranty Check.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed.
For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance
and service guide.
b.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.
5.  Verify that Chipset-TPM feature is enabled in the Trusted Platform Module options menu in System
Utilities.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Security%20module"/>
  </rdf:Description>
