    <diag:explanation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This fault occurs when the transport VIF for an I/O module is down. Cisco UCS Manager raises this fault when a fabric interconnect reports the connectivity state on virtual interface as one of the following: • Down • Errored • Unavailable</diag:explanation>
    <diag:sourcePage rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">94</diag:sourcePage>
    <diag:sourcePage rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">93</diag:sourcePage>
    <diag:causeCategory rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">cmc-vif-down</diag:causeCategory>
    <diag:eventName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">fltDcxVcMgmtVifDown</diag:eventName>
    <diag:eventCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">F0459</diag:eventCode>
    <diag:recordId rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0459</diag:recordId>
    <diag:recommendsProcedure rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0459/procedure/01"/>
    <diag:eventNamespace rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UCS-SEM</diag:eventNamespace>
    <diag:severity rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAJOR</diag:severity>
    <diag:hasCategory rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/category/Hardware%20Interconnect"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Processor"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Check that the system contains the latest available BIOS version.
Reseat the processor.
WARNING: To reduce the risk of personal injury from hot surfaces, allow the drives and the internal system
components to cool before touching them.
CAUTION: THE PINS ON THE SYSTEM BOARD ARE VERY FRAGILE AND EASILY DAMAGED. To avoid
damage to the system board, do not touch the processor or the processor socket contacts.
IMPORTANT: Both processor sockets must always be populated. If either processor socket is empty, the
server does not power up.
Reseat the DIMM.
1.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
2.  Disconnect each power cord from the server.
3.  Remove the DIMM.
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the
system board connector. See the Best Practices for Handling Memory Modules in ProLiant Server
Configurations (http://h20564.www2.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docId=emr_na-c00868283).
4.  Clean the DIMM and the DIMM slot with anti-static compressed air.
5.  Reinstall the DIMM.
For additional information, see the server maintenance and sever guide located at http://www.hpe.com/info/
enterprise/docs.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0215/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0215 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
