  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N11adee02386441adbfd15ea46d8db9a6">
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Be sure the drive data cable is working by replacing it with a known functional cable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Cable%20or%20connector"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0394/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0394/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0394/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0394/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Update to the latest firmware version.
Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more
information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an
accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each
of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are
available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation).
To update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide
and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses
Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components.
To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and
Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Warranty Status.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0394 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0394/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
