  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0027-0x0003/procedure/01">
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0027-0x0003/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0027-0x0003/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0027-0x0003/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0027-0x0003/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0027-0x0003/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0027-0x0003/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0027-0x0003/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0003 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Processor"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Power%20supply"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Check if the server power supply capacity or allocated server power is suitable for the workload.
1.  Check the server power supply capacity, for example, in the management processor Web GUI, under
Power and Thermal -&gt; Power, or Chassis Information for servers with chassis controlled power
supplies.
2.  Compare with the power consumption in the Power and Thermal -&gt; Power page, or if applicable, the
Power Meter page which provides up to 24 hours of power history in a graphical form.
3.  Increase the configured power cap value. If additional hardware has been added to the server, power
calibration during the next server boot may resolve this issue.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0266/procedure/01/cause">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#PossibleCause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0266 possible cause 1</rdfs:label>
