    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0378 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/011"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/014"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/012"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/009"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/010"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/015"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/017"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/013"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/016"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/018"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0378/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Processor"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To enable this NVDIMM, either install previously used processor if the processor has been changed recently,
or NVDIMM needs to be sanitized to configure it with the newly installed processor type.
If manual data backup of NVDIMM is desired, try installing previously used processor to take manual data
backup of NVDIMM. Chose desired system configuration afterward.
Sanitizing DIMMs
1.  From the System Utilities screen, select System Configuration &gt; BIOS/Platform Configuration
(RBSU) &gt; System Options &gt; Memory Operations &gt; NVDIMM Memory Options.
2.  Select NVDIMM-N Sanitize/Erase on Next Reboot Policy.
The following alert is displayed.
IMPORTANT: Sanitizing/Erasing an NVDIMM-N will result in the loss of ALL user data saved in the
NVDIMM-N. It is strongly recommended that manual backup of all user data in the NVDIMM-N(s) be
performed before sanitizing/erasing the NVDIMM-N(s).
3.  Press any key to proceed.
4.  Select one of the following menu items:
◦ Sanitize/Erase and Boot to Operating System
◦ Sanitize/Erase and Power System Off
◦ Sanitize/Erase and Boot to System Utilities
5.  Select one of the following menu items based on the NVDIMM-Ns to be sanitized/erased:
◦ Sanitize/Erase all NVDIMM-N in the System —Use this option for major system
reconfigurations.
◦ Sanitize/Erase all NVDIMM-N on Processor 1 —Use this option when all the NVDIMM-Ns on a
processor must be sanitized together, such as when enabling NVDIMM-N Memory Interleaving.
◦ Sanitize/Erase Processor 1 DIMM X —This option is available only when NVDIMM-N Memory
Interleaving is disabled. Use this option for adding individual NVDIMM-Ns, or for using an
NVDIMM-N again after errors occur.
◦ Sanitize/Erase all NVDIMM-N on Processor 2 —Use this option when all the NVDIMM-Ns on a
processor must be sanitized together, such as when enabling NVDIMM-N Memory Interleaving.
◦ Sanitize/Erase Processor 2 DIMM X —This option is available only when NVDIMM-N Memory
Interleaving is disabled. Use this option for adding individual NVDIMM-Ns, or for using an
NVDIMM-N again after errors occur.
When enabled, all user data in the selected NVDIMM-N is erased on the next reboot. The Sanitize
NVDIMM-N scope selections are available only after a sanitize policy is selected.
6.  Press the F10 key to save the changes.
7.  Reboot the server.
The server will reboot multiple times as part of the sanitize process. POST messages will also display
to indicate the NVDIMM-Ns that are being sanitized.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Warranty Status.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Na275962a8fc34dc3b2f84155ffb8638f">
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0233/procedure/01"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Re-seat the DIMMs in the identified channel and update the System ROM. Inspect DIMM sockets and the system board for bent pins or damaged traces. Perform the following procedure for each affected DIMM.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0233"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0233/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/System%20board"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PDR98">
    <diag:hasMessageTemplate rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PDR98/message/01"/>
    <diag:recommendsProcedure rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PDR98/procedure/01"/>
    <diag:sourcePage rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">1852</diag:sourcePage>
