    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0217/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0217/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0217/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0217/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0217/procedure/01/item/009"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0217/procedure/01/item/010"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reseat the processor.
WARNING: To reduce the risk of personal injury from hot surfaces, allow the drives and the internal system
components to cool before touching them.
CAUTION: THE PINS ON THE SYSTEM BOARD ARE VERY FRAGILE AND EASILY DAMAGED. To avoid
damage to the system board, do not touch the processor or the processor socket contacts.
IMPORTANT: Both processor sockets must always be populated. If either processor socket is empty, the
server does not power up.
Reseat the DIMM.
1.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
2.  Disconnect each power cord from the server.
3.  Remove the DIMM.
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the
system board connector. See the Best Practices for Handling Memory Modules in ProLiant Server
Configurations ( http://h20564.www2.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docId=emr_na-c00868283).
4.  Clean the DIMM and the DIMM slot with anti-static compressed air.
5.  Reinstall the DIMM.
For more information, see the server maintenance and service guide for your product on the Hewlett
Packard Enterprise website:
•  HPE ProLiant Gen10 (http://www.hpe.com/info/proliantgen10-docs)
•  HPE Synergy (http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs)
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Processor"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0217/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0217 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
