  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/011"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/012"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/010"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/009"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/013"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0029/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0029 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Replace the power supply.
1.  Be sure no loose connections exist. For more information, see Resolving loose connections in the
Troubleshooting Guide for HPE ProLiant Gen10 servers.
2.  If the power supplies have LEDs, be sure they indicate that each power supply is working properly.
a.  The LEDs indicate an issue with a power supply (red, amber, or off), then check the power
source.
b.  If the power source is working properly, then replace the power supply.
c.  Be sure the system has enough power, particularly if you recently added hardware, such
as drives. Remove the newly added component and if the issue is no longer present, then
additional power supplies are required. Check the system information from the IML.
▪ For product-specific information, see the server documentation at http://www.hpe.com/
info/enterprise/docs.
▪ For more information on Power Advisor, go to http://www.hpe.com/info/poweradvisor.
▪ Refer to the Integrated Management Log for details.
3.  If running a redundant configuration, be sure that the installed power supplies in the system
meet system redundancy requirements. For a list of supported power supplies, see the server
documentation (http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs).
4.  For further troubleshooting, see the Power-on issues flowchart in the Troubleshooting Guide for HPE
ProLiant Gen10 servers.
For more information, see the server documentation (http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs).
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
