  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1914/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If the drive is part of a fault-tolerant volume
1.  Verify that the Volume Status is OK.
2.  Replace the drive.
If the drive is not part of a fault-tolerant volume
1.  Back up all data.
2.  Replace the drive.
3.  Reconfigure the RAID.
4.  Restore data from the backup.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Check Status under the Warranty Check
heading.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x1914 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1914/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1914/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
