    <diag:addressesCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-STOR394/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [409, 704); FULL_TEXT_SOURCE_MARKERS; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: SOURCE_ANCHORED_RULE_LINK. Explicit action verb and shared documented component/condition in the same source group; inferred intended purpose only.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If the issue persists, remove the NVMe drive identified in the message, and replace it with a working drive. If the issue is not resolved, contact your service provider. For more information about repairing issues in NVMe drives, see the relevant PERC Users Guide available on the support site.</diag:itemText>
  </rdf:Description>
