    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 237); UNNUMBERED_SOURCE_BLOCK; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: ESCALATION_OR_SUPPORT. Support escalation or collection instructions are not treated as a repair of the cause.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If the issue persists, Collect a SupportAssist collection (TSR) report using iDRAC. Visit https:// www.dell.com/support/incidents-online/contactus/dynamic to use the Virtual Assistant to analyze the collection and recommend a resolution.</diag:itemText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-SCV019/procedure/01/item/001">
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the existing Delta certificate, upload the latest certificate that has the consolidated data, and then retry the operation. For more information about SCV, see the Secured Component Verification (SCV) Reference Guide available on the support site.</diag:itemText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dell SCV019 printed item 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: AMBIGUOUS_CORRESPONDENCE. An action exists, but its target cannot be tied to the documented cause by the conservative rules.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 254); UNNUMBERED_SOURCE_BLOCK; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
