  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0014-0x0016/procedure/01">
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/System%20board"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Battery%20or%20capacitor"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Processor"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Review all error messages for possible issues with other components and troubleshoot the identified
components using the following procedure:
1.  Verify that no loose connections exist on the system board or power backplane. It is not necessary to
reseat processors. For more information, see Resolving loose connections.
2.  Remove the mezzanine card that was recently added. For more information on removal and
replacement procedures, see the Product Maintenance and Service Guide (http://www.hpe.com/info/
enterprise/docs).
3.  Power down to remove the power completely from the server. Remove the system battery for 10
minutes.
4.  Reinstall the battery and power on the server. To locate the system battery and for server-specific
procedures, see the product documentation (http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs).
5.  Reset NVRAM to default setting using the BIOS utility (F9). If the system does not boot, use System
Maintenance Switch, SW6, to reset NVRAM. For more information, see the label on the server access
panel or the Server User Guide.
6.  Gather necessary information and contact support.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0014-0x0016/procedure/01/item/005"/>
