    <diag:explanation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A redundant virtual disk has lost redundancy. This may occur when the virtual disk suffers the failure of more than one physical disk. In this case, both the source physical disk and the target disk with redundant data have failed. A rebuild is not possible because there is no longer redundancy.</diag:explanation>
