  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1914/procedure/01/item/001">
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x1914 printed item 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: ESCALATION_OR_SUPPORT. Warranty/support administration is not a cause-specific diagnosis or corrective operation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 806); UNNUMBERED_SOURCE_BLOCK; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If the drive is part of a fault-tolerant volume 1. Verify that the Volume Status is OK. 2. Replace the drive. If the drive is not part of a fault-tolerant volume 1. Back up all data. 2. Replace the drive. 3. Reconfigure the RAID. 4. Restore data from the backup. If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case. 1. Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Check Status under the Warranty Check heading. This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service guide. 2. Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case. HPE Support will contact you.</diag:itemText>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">1</diag:itemOrder>
  </rdf:Description>
