    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0008-0x0004/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  Go to https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home.
2.  Under Documentation and Software, click Knowledge Base.
3.  Enter System ROM 2.20 in the search bar, and then click search.
4.  Click Drivers and Software.
5.  Under Operating System, select the correct operating system.
6.  Under Software Type, select BIOS (Entitlement Required).
7.  Under Software Subtype, select System ROM.
8.  Select the appropriate patch, and then click Download.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Warranty Status.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0004 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
