    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If you see this fault, create a show tech-support file and contact Cisco TAC.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Nd86f066600fb46a4a2dedb113b9de29a">
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PWR2254/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PWR2254"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PWR2254/procedure/01"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Check for unacknowledged use of 110V and change to acknowledged. Using the Chassis Management Controller/Management Module (CMC/MM) web interface, select Chassis Overview&gt;Power&gt;Configuration and then check the 110V Acknowledge field. Retry the operation to turn on the server.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0338/procedure/01/item/003">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0338 printed item 3</rdfs:label>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: AMBIGUOUS_CORRESPONDENCE. An action exists, but its target cannot be tied to the documented cause by the conservative rules.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [246, 290); FULL_TEXT_SOURCE_MARKERS; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Select Yes, restore the default settings.</diag:itemText>
    <diag:sourceLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.</diag:sourceLabel>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">3</diag:itemOrder>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0482/procedure/01/item/001">
    <diag:investigatesCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0482/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Verify firmware image and retry the firmware update. Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation). To update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components. To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs. If the issues persists, replace the NVDIMM.</diag:itemText>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 1013); ACTIONABLE_SOURCE_PREFIX; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: SOURCE_ANCHORED_RULE_LINK. Explicit action verb and shared documented component/condition in the same source group; inferred intended purpose only.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">1</diag:itemOrder>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0482 printed item 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x2424/procedure/01/item/001">
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">1</diag:itemOrder>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 125); UNNUMBERED_SOURCE_BLOCK; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: AMBIGUOUS_CORRESPONDENCE. An action exists, but its target cannot be tied to the documented cause by the conservative rules.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Restore NIC factory defaults. For more information, see your system documentation at http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs.</diag:itemText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x2424 printed item 1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-UEFI0434/procedure/01">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dell UEFI0434 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
