  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x003F/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Install supported Smart Storage Energy Pack and ensure energy pack cable is well seated. Confirm energy
pack status in the iLO GUI.
See the HPE Smart Storage Battery issues for Smart Array controllers section in the Troubleshooting Guide
for HPE ProLiant Gen10 servers guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs.
See the iLO 5 documentation for information on confirming the energy pack status.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x003F/procedure/01/item/001"/>
