    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Processor"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Reseat the processor. WARNING: To reduce the risk of personal injury from hot surfaces, allow the drives and the internal system components to cool before touching them. CAUTION: THE PINS ON THE SYSTEM BOARD ARE VERY FRAGILE AND EASILY DAMAGED. To avoid damage to the system board, do not touch the processor or the processor socket contacts. Important: Only authorized technicians trained by Hewlett Packard Enterprise should attempt to remove or replace a processor. If you believe the processor requires replacement, contact Hewlett Packard Enterprise technical support before proceeding. Create a Hewlett Packard Enterprise Support Case.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
