  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-379/procedure/01/cause">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 379 possible cause 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#PossibleCause"/>
    <diag:causeText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The server does not match the original server in which the NVDIMM was used, and NVDIMM-N Memory
Interleaving is disabled.
CAUTION:
Before removing or replacing any processors, be sure to follow the guidelines
in "Processor troubleshooting guidelines" in the troubleshooting guide for your
product. Failure to follow the recommended guidelines can cause damage to the
system board, requiring replacement of the system board.</diag:causeText>
  </rdf:Description>
