    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Disconnect each power cord from the server CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system board connector. See the DIMM handling guidelines on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Library at: http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs 2. Swap the DIMMs . If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case. 1. Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the: Customer Self Repair website. This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service guide. 2. Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc. HPE Support will contact you.</diag:itemText>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [293, 1040); FULL_TEXT_SOURCE_MARKERS; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: PREPARATORY_OR_NAVIGATION. Setup/navigation or power isolation alone is not a cause-specific diagnosis or repair.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0565 printed item 3</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
