  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1788/procedure/02">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1788/procedure/02/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1788/procedure/02/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1788/procedure/02/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1788/procedure/02/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1788/procedure/02/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1788/procedure/02/item/001"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1788/procedure/02/cause"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  If a bad power cable connection exists:
•  Repair the connection, and then press the F2 key.
•  If the issue persists, run HPE SSA.
For more information, see the HPE Smart Storage Administrator User Guide on the Hewlett
Packard Enterprise website (https://www.hpe.com/info/smartstorage-docs).
2.  Be sure that the cable is routed correctly.
For more information, see the server user guide for your product on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise
website:
•  HPE ProLiant Gen10 (https://www.hpe.com/info/proliantgen10-docs)
•  HPE Synergy (https://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs)</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Cable%20or%20connector"/>
    <diag:procedureLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Solution 2</diag:procedureLabel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 1788 recommendation 2</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-Windows-cpqstmsg-dll-1164/message/01">
    <diag:messageText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The Drive Array Controller in slot %4 has a new status of %5.</diag:messageText>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#MessageTemplate"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 1164 message 1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1735/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1735/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1735/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Do one of the following:
•  Disconnect the redundant SAS cables.
•  Update the firmware.
Update to the latest firmware version.
Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more
information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an
accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each
of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are
available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation).
To update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide
and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses
Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components.
To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and
Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x1735 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
