    <diag:sourceLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1)</diag:sourceLabel>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">1</diag:itemOrder>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If a physical disk was removed from the disk group, either replace the disk or restore the original disk. Identify the disk that was removed by locating the disk that has a red "X" for its status.</diag:itemText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-UEFI0033/procedure/01/item/001">
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">1</diag:itemOrder>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 231); UNNUMBERED_SOURCE_BLOCK; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: NO_DOCUMENTED_CAUSE. No documented cause in this source solution group; do not invent a cause.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dell UEFI0033 printed item 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To change the system BIOS settings and persistently save the settings, revert the hardware setting identified in the message to the previous state and then go to the System Setup &gt; System BIOS page to configure the system settings.</diag:itemText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1733/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1733/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1733/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1733/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x1733 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Do the following:
Option 1: Upgrade the enclosure firmware and the controller firmware.
Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more
information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an
accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each
of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are
available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation).
To update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide
and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses
Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components.
To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and
Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.
For specific instructions on updating firmware, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide, at http://
www.hpe.com/info/hpsum/documentation.
Option 2: If the issue persists, create an HPE Support Case and replace the affected enclosure components.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1733/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PSU0047/procedure/01/item/002">
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reinstall the PSU and reconnect the cord.</diag:itemText>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
