  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1703/procedure/01">
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1703/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1703/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1703/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1703/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1703/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1703/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1703/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 1703 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  Upgrade to the latest firmware.
For more information, see the following topic in the troubleshooting guide for your product on the
Hewlett Packard Enterprise website:
•  HPE ProLiant Gen10—"Keeping the system current" (https://www.hpe.com/info/gen10-
troubleshooting)
•  HPE Synergy—"Updating the firmware" (https://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-troubleshooting)
2.  If the issue persists, replace the cache module or controller.
For more information, see the server maintenance and service guide for your product on the Hewlett
Packard Enterprise website:
•  HPE ProLiant Gen10 (https://www.hpe.com/info/proliantgen10-docs)
•  HPE Synergy (https://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs)</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1794/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1794/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1794/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1794/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If you see this fault, take the following actions:
1. Wait a few minutes to see if the fault clears. This is typically a temporary issue, and can occur after a
firmware upgrade.
2. If the above action did not resolve the issue, create a show tech-support file and contact Cisco TAC.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cisco F1794 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N496ddb57fc8d4576a7d1e2b39de85237">
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Storage%20controller"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Run SUT from the command line (On-Demand mode) to update the Smart Array firmware. For more information, see to the HP SUT documents at http://www.hpe.com/info/sut-docs. Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP): Update the Smart Array firmware by downloading the SPP from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Refer to the SPP documentation at http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/ documentation for instructions on updating the firmware. Note: Downloading an SPP requires a contract with Hewlett Packard Enterprise and an HPE Passport ID. If you do not have an HPE Passport ID, go to http://www.hpe.com/info/insightonline. Note: Downloading the entire SPP can take a significant amount of time. Online Flash components This component provides updated system firmware that can be installed directly on supported operating systems. Additionally, when used in conjunction with the SUM, this Smart Component allows you to update firmware on remote servers from a central location. This remote deployment capability eliminates the need for you to be physically present at the server to perform a firmware update. For specific instructions on updating firmware, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide, at http:// www.hpe.com/info/hpsum/documentation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1809/procedure/01/item/013"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1809"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1809/procedure/01"/>
  </rdf:Description>
