  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/009"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/014"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/012"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/013"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/011"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/010"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0261/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Storage%20controller"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0261 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Update firmware
There are multiple ways to upgrade the firmware:
HPE Support website:
1.  Go to https://www.hpe.com/us/en/support.html.
2.  Click HPE Storage, Servers and Networking.
3.  Enter product name, and then click Go.
4.  Click Get drivers, software, and firmware.
5.  Select the appropriate operating system.
6.  Click the Firmware-Storage Controller category.
7.  Locate, download, and install the latest firmware.
Smart Update Manager (SUM):
1.  Download SUM from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/hpsum/
download).
2.  Be sure you have the latest SPP (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp/download).
3.  Open SUM and add the baseline that includes the Smart Array driver. For specific instructions on
updating firmware, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide, at http://www.hpe.com/info/hpsum/
documentation.
Smart Update Tool (SUT):
Note: To use SUT, you must have HPE OneView downloaded and installed. For more information, see the
HPE OneView documentation at http://www.hpe.com/info/ovvcenter/docs.
1.  Download SUT from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/info/hpsut).
2.  Be sure you have the latest SPP (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp/download).
3.  Run SUT from the command line (On-Demand mode) to update the Smart Array firmware. For more
information, see to the HP SUT documents at http://www.hpe.com/info/sut-docs.
Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP):
Update the Smart Array firmware by downloading the SPP from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise
website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Refer to the SPP documentation at http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/
documentation for instructions on updating the firmware.
Note: Downloading an SPP requires a contract with Hewlett Packard Enterprise and an HPE Passport ID. If
you do not have an HPE Passport ID, go to http://www.hpe.com/info/insightonline.
Note: Downloading the entire SPP can take a significant amount of time.
Online Flash components
This component provides updated system firmware that can be installed directly on supported operating
systems. Additionally, when used in conjunction with the SUM, this Smart Component allows you to update
firmware on remote servers from a central location.
This remote deployment capability eliminates the need for you to be physically present at the server to
perform a firmware update.
For specific instructions on updating firmware, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide, at http://
www.hpe.com/info/hpsum/documentation.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
