    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Possible actions:
•  Verify that Cache module is seated correctly. Replace if necessary. Select Ignore to persist with this
message on reboots until failed paths are restored. Select Repair to disable this message on reboots
- no further POST message for recurring path failure with logical drive(s) corresponding to these disk
drives.
•  Verify that Cache module is seated correctly. Replace if necessary. Select Ignore to persist with this
message on reboots until failed paths are restored. Select Repair to disable this message on reboots
- no further POST message for recurring path failure with logical drive(s) corresponding to these disk
drives.
•  Verify failed disks using HP SSA and replace as necessary. Select Ignore to persist with this message
on reboots until failed paths are restored. Select Repair to disable this message on reboots - no
further POST message for recurring path failure with logical drive(s) corresponding to these disk
drives.
•  Verify that Cache module is seated correctly. Replace if necessary. Select Ignore to persist with this
message on reboots until failed paths are restored. Select Repair to disable this message on reboots
- no further POST message for recurring path failure with logical drive(s) corresponding to these disk
drives
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x1769 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
