  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0543/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0543/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0543/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0543/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cisco F0543 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If you see this fault, take the following actions:
1. Verify that the capability catalog in Cisco UCS Manager is up to date. If necessary, update the catalog.
2. Verify if supported chassis is installed.
3. If the above action did not resolve the issue, execute the show tech-support command and contact Cisco
technical support.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0543/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0565/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0565 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Processor"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0565/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0565/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0565/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0565/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PMems must be installed on the black DIMM slot when on the same channel as a RDIMM/LRDIMM. Swap
the DIMMs in Slots %1 and %2 on Processor %3. Review documentation for more information on supported
configurations.
1.  Remove all power.
a.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
b.  Disconnect each power cord from the server
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system
board connector. See the DIMM handling guidelines on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Library at:
http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs
2.  Swap the DIMMs .
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
