    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1945/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1945/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1945/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x1945 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  Create and HPE Support case to replace the faulty drives:
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Check Status under the Warranty
Check heading.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed.
For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance
and service guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.
2.  After you receive the replacement drives.
3.  Remove all power.
a.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
b.  Disconnect each power cord from the server
4.  Replace failed drives indicated by the error.
5.  Replace missing drives indicated by the error.
6.  Be sure no loose connections exist. For more information, see "Resolving loose connections" in the
Troubleshooting Guide.
7.  Allow sufficient time for rebuild to complete.
8.  Check storage software for further details.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
