    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x3143/procedure/01/item/011"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x3143/procedure/01/item/014"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x3143 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x3143/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  Retry encryption enablement with the correct passphrase.
1.  Reboot the system, and then press F9 when the POST screen is displayed.
2.  Press F9.
The System Utilities page is displayed.
3.  Select BIOS/Platform Configuration (RBSU).
4.  Select Server Security.
5.  Select Device Encryption Options.
6.  Select Device Encryption Settings.
7.  Select Encrypted Devices.
8.  Select appropriate device under Select Device.
9.  Select Modify Passphrase in the Select Operation box.
10.  Select Auto or Manual in the Passphrase Type box.
11.  If using Manual Passphrase Type, enter your passphrase in the Passphrase box.
12.  Click Start Operation.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
