  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1779/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1779/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1779/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1779/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1779/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1779/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1779/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1779/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-1779/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 1779 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Procedure
1.  Do one of the following:
•  Press the F1 key to continue with logical drives disabled.
•  Press the F2 key to accept data loss and re-enable logical drives.
2.  Resolve any issues that disabled the drive.
3.  If the drive is replaced, restore data from the backup.
Results
Be sure the system is always powered up and down correctly:
•  When powering up the system, all external storage systems must be powered up before (or at the same
time as) the server.
•  When powering down the system, the server must be powered down before powering down any external
storage systems.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
