    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1920/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1920/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1920/procedure/01/item/011"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1920/procedure/01/item/010"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x1920 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Fan issue
1.  Follow the procedures and warnings in the server documentation for removing the access panels and
accessing and replacing fans.
2.  Unseat, and then reseat, each fan according to the proper procedures.
3.  Replace the access panels, and then attempt to restart the server.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Check Status under the Warranty Check
heading.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.
Supply issue
Create a Hewlett Packard Enterprise support case and replace the power supply.
Enclosure Processor issue
Power cycle storage enclosure.
Update the enclosure firmware.
1.  Go to https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home.
2.  Under Documentation and Software, click Knowledge Base.
3.  Enter System ROM 2.20 in the search bar, and then click search.
4.  Click Drivers and Software.
5.  Under Operating System, select the correct operating system.
6.  Under Software Type, select BIOS (Entitlement Required).
7.  Under Software Subtype, select System ROM.
8.  Select the appropriate patch, and then click Download.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Check Status under the Warranty Check
heading.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
