    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">5</diag:itemOrder>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: SOURCE_ANCHORED_RULE_LINK. Explicit action verb and shared documented component/condition in the same source group; inferred intended purpose only.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [772, 1009); FULL_TEXT_SOURCE_MARKERS; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reset the NVRAM to default using the BIOS utility (F9). If the system fails to boot, then use System Maintenance Switch, SW6, to reset the NVRAM. For more information, see the label on the server access panel or the server user guide.</diag:itemText>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x000A printed item 5</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Na0c6c559629b4d238f682daf02a2d38c">
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Management%20controller"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Update the latest iDRAC firmware version on the server and retry the operation. To update iDRAC by using iDRAC GUI, click (Maintenance &gt; System Update &gt; Manual Update). By using RACADM, run the following at the Command Line Interface (CLI): "racadm update".</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
