  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0029-0x0002/procedure/01">
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_SYSTEM_BOARD, 2, 0), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: Reseat Boot Drive 1
2. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_SYSTEM_BOARD, 2, 1), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: Reseat Boot Drive 2
3. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 0, 0), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
4. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 0, 2), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
5. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 0, 7), EVT_CRITICAL ,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: replace IOM.
This is not a customer serviceable part, so if the cable isn’t installed the IOM is not assembled correctly. HBA
Slot 1 won’t work
6. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 1, 0), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
7. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 1, 2), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
8. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 1, 7), EVT_CRITICAL ,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: replace IOM.
This is not a customer serviceable part, so if the cable isn’t installed the IOM is not assembled correctly. HBA
Slot 2 won’t work
9. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 2, 0), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
10. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 2, 2), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
11. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 2, 7), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: this is complicated, there is no easy message here. On a JBOF Cables 3 and 4 are not
supposed to be installed, but on a node they are. So if these aren’t installed on a node then Node is incorrect
but on a JBOF it is expected. This is why this is informational and not critical.
12. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 3, 0), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
13. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 3, 2), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
14. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 3, 7), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: this is complicated, there is no easy message here. On a JBOF Cables 3 and 4 are not
supposed to be installed, but on a node they are. So if these aren’t installed on a node then Node is incorrect
but on a JBOF it is expected. This is why this is informational and not critical.
15. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_MEZZ_CARD, 0, 0), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
16. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_MISCELLANEOUS, 2, 0), EVT_CRITICAL ,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: replace IOM.
This is not a customer serviceable part, so if the LOM isn’t installed the IOM is not assembled correctly. The
ETH ports on the IOM won’t work.
17. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_MISCELLANEOUS, 2, 1), EVT_CRITICAL ,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: replace IOM.
This is not a customer serviceable part, so if the 7-seg isn’t installed the IOM is not assembled correctly. The
7-segment display won’t work.
18. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_MISCELLANEOUS, 2, 2), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: None.
This should never assert as the fan blank was never productized in Raider.
19. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_MISCELLANEOUS, 2, 3), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.
Some Raider Personas (like RC) don’t use the CDM, so this is really informational, even though Arcus uses it.
20. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_MISCELLANEOUS, 2, 4), EVT_CRITICAL ,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: Replace Chassis.
This is not a customer serviceable part, so if the TSB isn’t installed the Chassis is not assembled correctly.
The LEDs/temp sensor in the rack ear won’t work.
21. Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_MISCELLANEOUS, 2, 7), EVT_INFORMATIONAL,
EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE },
Recommended Action: none – this is just informational.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0002 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
