  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F1284/procedure/01/cause">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cisco F1284 possible cause 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#PossibleCause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:causeText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This fault typically occurs for the following reasons: when Auto Firmware Sync Policy is set Auto-acknowledge or User-acknowledge and default host firmware pack is not available. • Auto Firmware Sync is not happening. • Default host firmware package is missing or deleted.</diag:causeText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0002-0x0024/procedure/01/item/017">
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [2307, 2568); FULL_TEXT_SOURCE_MARKERS; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: ESCALATION_OR_SUPPORT. Warranty/support administration is not a cause-specific diagnosis or corrective operation.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case. HPE Support will contact you. For more information on adding or replacing a fan, see the server maintenance and service guide for your product on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website:</diag:itemText>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <diag:sourceLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.</diag:sourceLabel>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">17</diag:itemOrder>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0024 printed item 17</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-SWC5012/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-SWC5012/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-SWC5012/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dell SWC5012 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Do the following:1) There is a cable or connection issue. Begin by identifying the issue:1a) Review
the Lifecycle Log for any Hardware Configuration (HWC) events that may be reported shortly after
this event. If the system can identify the cable or component causing this issue, it will report a
configuration error.1b) Reference the System Information Label on the chassis cover or the Cable
Routing section in the Installation and Service Manual (ISM). If the HWC message was located, look
for references to that connection, cable, or device.Else, if the message references an SL cable, use
the SL cable referenced in the message to locate the connector on the motherboard. This will be
used to trace the cable to the end device. Else, if the message references a critical cable, locate the
specified cable path and associated components.1c) If any maintenanceor service work was recently
completed and SWC5012 was not present before this activity, something is likely disconnected in that
area.2) Proceed withcorrection:2a) Disconnect the power cords.2b) Use the information gathered
above to locate the impacted cable or device.Else, if the message references an SL cable, locate the
SL cable connector on the motherboard and trace the cable to the end device. Else, if the message
references a critical cable, locate the specified cable path and associated components.2c)If the
message references an SL cable,ensure that the device is firmly seated and, if it has any power, signal,
and SL cables, ensure they are connected and firmly seated on both ends and there is no physical
damage.If the message references a critical cable, ensure that the critical cable is connected and
firmly seated on both ends and there is no physical damage.2d) Close the chassis cover and reconnect
the power cords.2e) If the issue persists, collect a SupportAssist collection (TSR) report using iDRAC.
Visithttps://www.dell.com/support/incidents-online/contactus/dynamicto use the Virtual Assistant
to analyze the collection and recommend a resolution.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-SWC5012/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Cable%20or%20connector"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
  </rdf:Description>
