    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0212 printed item 3</rdfs:label>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the DIMM. CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system board connector. See the Best Practices for Handling Memory Modules in ProLiant Server Configurations ( http://h20564.www2.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docId=emr_na-c00868283).</diag:itemText>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">3</diag:itemOrder>
    <diag:sourceLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3.</diag:sourceLabel>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: AMBIGUOUS_CORRESPONDENCE. An action exists, but its target cannot be tied to the documented cause by the conservative rules.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [104, 396); FULL_TEXT_SOURCE_MARKERS; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
