    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/013"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/012"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/021"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/017"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/020"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/014"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/015"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0373/procedure/01/item/016"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To continue to use the previously functioning interleaved set, reinstall the NVDIMM.
1.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
2.  Disconnect each power cord from the server.
3.  Remove the NVDIMM.
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle NVDIMMs can cause damage to NVDIMM components and the
system board connector. See the Best Practices for Handling Memory Modules in ProLiant Server
Configurations ( http://h20564.www2.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docId=emr_na-c00868283).
4.  Clean the NVDIMM and the NVDIMM slot with anti-static compressed air.
5.  Reinstall the NVDIMM.
For additional information, see the server maintenance and sever guide located at http://www.hpe.com/info/
enterprise/docs.
If the issue persists, sanitize the NVDIMM:
1.  From the System Utilities screen, select System Configuration &gt; BIOS/Platform Configuration
(RBSU) &gt; System Options &gt; Memory Operations &gt; NVDIMM Memory Options.
2.  Select NVDIMM-N Sanitize/Erase on Next Reboot Policy.
The following alert is displayed.
IMPORTANT: Sanitizing/Erasing an NVDIMM-N will result in the loss of ALL user data saved in the
NVDIMM-N. Hewlett Packard Enterprise recommends that manual backup of all user data in the
NVDIMM-Ns be performed before sanitizing/erasing the NVDIMM-Ns.
3.  Press any key to proceed.
4.  Select one of the following menu items:
◦ Sanitize/Erase and Boot to Operating System
◦ Sanitize/Erase and Power System Off
◦ Sanitize/Erase and Boot to System Utilities
5.  Select one of the following menu items based on the NVDIMM-Ns to be sanitized/erased:
◦ Sanitize/Erase all NVDIMM-N in the System —Use this option for major system
reconfigurations.
◦ Sanitize/Erase all NVDIMM-N on Processor 1 —Use this option when all the NVDIMM-Ns on a
processor must be sanitized together, such as when enabling NVDIMM-N Memory Interleaving.
◦ Sanitize/Erase Processor 1 DIMM X —This option is available only when NVDIMM-N Memory
Interleaving is disabled. Use this option for adding individual NVDIMM-Ns, or for using an
NVDIMM-N again after errors occur.
◦ Sanitize/Erase all NVDIMM-N on Processor 2 —Use this option when all the NVDIMM-Ns on a
processor must be sanitized together, such as when enabling NVDIMM-N Memory Interleaving.
◦ Sanitize/Erase Processor 2 DIMM X —This option is available only when NVDIMM-N Memory
Interleaving is disabled. Use this option for adding individual NVDIMM-Ns, or for using an
NVDIMM-N again after errors occur.
When enabled, all user data in the selected NVDIMM-N is erased on the next reboot. The Sanitize
NVDIMM-N scope selections are available only after a sanitize policy is selected.
6.  Press the F10 key to save the changes.
7.  Reboot the server.
The server will reboot multiple times as part of the sanitize process. POST messages will also display
to indicate the NVDIMM-Ns that are being sanitized.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Warranty Status.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
