  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0237 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0237/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove and replace any incompatible DIMMs. Ensure that all installed DIMMs are the same type.
1.  Remove all power.
a.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
b.  Disconnect each power cord from the server
2.  Remove the DIMM.
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system
board connector. See the DIMM handling guidelines on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Library at:
http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs
3.  Install the new DIMM.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
