    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0037/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0037/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0037/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0037 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Before you add a power supply or replace the failed power supply, do the following:
1.  Be sure no loose connections exist.
2.  If the power supplies have LEDs, be sure they indicate that each power supply is working properly.
◦ If the LEDs indicate an issue with a power supply (red, amber, or off), then check the power
source.
◦ If the power source is working properly, then replace the power supply.
3.  Be sure the system has enough power, particularly if you recently added hardware, such as drives.
Remove the newly added component. If the issue is no longer present, then additional power supplies
are required.
4.  If running a redundant configuration, be sure that the installed power supplies in the system meet
system redundancy requirements.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Power%20supply"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0037/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
