    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Sanitize/Erase Processor 2 DIMM X —This option is available only when NVDIMM-N Memory Interleaving is disabled. Use this option for adding individual NVDIMM-Ns, or for using an NVDIMM-N again after errors occur. When enabled, all user data in the selected NVDIMM-N is erased on the next reboot. The Sanitize NVDIMM-N scope selections are available only after a sanitize policy is selected.</diag:itemText>
  </rdf:Description>
