    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0028-0x0001/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Re-seat the USB drive key.
1.  Be sure that USB is enabled in the UEFI System Utilities.
2.  Be sure the drive boot order in the UEFI System Utilities is set so that the server boots from the USB
drive key.
3.  Re-seat the USB drive key.
4.  Move the USB drive key to a different USB port, if available.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
