  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0408/procedure/01">
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">If you see this fault, take the following actions:
1. In Cisco UCS Manager, verify that all PSUs for the chassis are functional.
2. Verify that all PSUs are seated properly within the chassis and are powered on.
3. Physically unplug and replug the power cord into the chassis.
4. If all PSUs are operating at maximum capacity, either add more PSUs to the chassis or redefine the power
policy in Cisco UCS Manager.
5. If the above actions did not resolve the issue, create a show tech-support file and contact Cisco TAC.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0408/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/CISCO-UCS-6-UCS-SEM-F0408/procedure/01/item/002"/>
