  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x3134/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x3134/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x3134/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x3134 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Retry the secure erase operation.
CAUTION: Secure erase should be used with extreme caution, and only when a system is being
decommissioned. The secure erase process resets iLO and deletes all licenses stored there, resets BIOS
settings, and deletes all AHS and warranty data stored on the system. The secure erase process also erases
supported non-volatile storage data and deletes any deployment settings profiles. iLO reboots multiple
times during the process.
CAUTION: Disconnect any FCoE, iSCSI, external SAS, and fibre channel storage before using secure erase.
For additional information, see Intelligent Provisioning 3.x - Using Secure Erase and Reset.
If the issue persists, update the Trusted Platform Module firmware.
Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more
information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an
accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each
of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are
available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation).
To update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide
and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses
Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components.
To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and
Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.
If this issue persists create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x3134/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
