  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0029-0x0002/procedure/01/item/011">
    <diag:sourceLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">11.</diag:sourceLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: CONTEXT_OR_REFERENCE. No recognised diagnostic/corrective instruction in this printed item.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [2152, 2591); FULL_TEXT_SOURCE_MARKERS; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">11</diag:itemOrder>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Interlock_mon.c (vrd\src): { ICT_FAULT_KEY(ICT_IO_PCIe_SLOTS, 2, 7), EVT_INFORMATIONAL, EVT_CLASS_INTERLOCK, EVT_IL_DEV_INSTALLED_STATE }, Recommended Action: this is complicated, there is no easy message here. On a JBOF Cables 3 and 4 are not supposed to be installed, but on a node they are. So if these aren’t installed on a node then Node is incorrect but on a JBOF it is expected. This is why this is informational and not critical.</diag:itemText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0002 printed item 11</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
