  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/009"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1912/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  Check the fans and be sure the air flows over the drive.
2.  Install the access panel, if removed.
3.  Install any missing drive blanks.
4.  Be sure no loose connections exist. For more information, see the Resolving loose connections
section in the Troubleshooting Guide for HPE ProLiant Gen10 servers at http://www.hpe.com/info/
Gen10-troubleshooting.
5.  Be sure the drive or backplane is cabled properly.
6.  Be sure the drive data cable is working by replacing it with a known functional cable.
7.  Be sure drive blanks are installed properly when the server is operating. Drives may overheat and
cause sluggish response or drive failure.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case:
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Check Status under the Warranty Check
heading.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
