  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reseat the indicated DIMM.
1.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
2.  Disconnect each power cord from the server.
3.  Remove the DIMM.
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the
system board connector. See the Best Practices for Handling Memory Modules in ProLiant Server
Configurations (http://h20564.www2.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docId=emr_na-c00868283).
4.  Clean the DIMM and the DIMM slot with anti-static compressed air.
5.  Reinstall the DIMM.
For additional information, see the server maintenance and sever guide located at http://www.hpe.com/info/
enterprise/docs.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Warranty Status.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0461 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0461/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x2426/procedure/01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x2426/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x2426 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x2426/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Update to the latest firmware version.
Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more
information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an
accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each
of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are
available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation).
To update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide
and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses
Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components.
To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and
Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
