    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0218 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Caution: Before removing or replacing any processors, be sure to follow the guidelines in "Processor
troubleshooting guidelines" in the troubleshooting guide for your product. Failure to follow the
recommended guidelines can cause damage to the system board, requiring replacement of the system
board.
Important: Gen10 processors must be removed and replaced by an HPE approved vendor.
1.  Remove and then reinstall the specified DIMMs and processors.
For more information, see the server maintenance and service guide for your product on the Hewlett
Packard Enterprise website:
◦ HPE ProLiant Gen10 (http://www.hpe.com/info/proliantgen10-docs)
◦ HPE Synergy (http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs)
2.  If the issue persists, replace the specified DIMMs.
1.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
2.  Disconnect each power cord from the server.
3.  Remove the DIMM.
CAUTION: See the DIMM handling guidelines on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Library at:
http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs.
For DIMM population, see the Population rules for memory with HPE ProLiant and Synergy
Gen10 servers http://www.hpe.com/docs/memory-population-rules.
4.  Install the new DIMM.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to
https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click Warranty Status.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Under Support Cases, click Access Cases, and then create a support case.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Processor"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
  </rdf:Description>
