  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0367/procedure/01/item/013">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0367 printed item 13</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [1193, 2458); FULL_TEXT_SOURCE_MARKERS; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: AMBIGUOUS_CORRESPONDENCE. An action exists, but its target cannot be tied to the documented cause by the conservative rules.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:sourceLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3.</diag:sourceLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">13</diag:itemOrder>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Run SUT from the command line (On-Demand mode) to update the Smart Array firmware. For more information, see to the HP SUT documents at http://www.hpe.com/info/sut-docs. Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP): Update the Smart Array firmware by downloading the SPP from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Refer to the SPP documentation at http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/ documentation for instructions on updating the firmware. Note: Downloading an SPP requires a contract with Hewlett Packard Enterprise and an HPE Passport ID. If you do not have an HPE Passport ID, go to http://www.hpe.com/info/insightonline. Note: Downloading the entire SPP can take a significant amount of time. Online Flash components This component provides updated system firmware that can be installed directly on supported operating systems. Additionally, when used in conjunction with the SUM, this Smart Component allows you to update firmware on remote servers from a central location. This remote deployment capability eliminates the need for you to be physically present at the server to perform a firmware update. For specific instructions on updating firmware, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide, at http:// www.hpe.com/info/hpsum/documentation.</diag:itemText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Ndf23f56592954e1484b62215b17bb09b">
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1811/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1811"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Storage%20controller"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1811/procedure/01"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: If the issue persists, update the iLO, Smart Array, and System ROM to the latest versions. To update the firmware on HPE ProLiant servers, see Keeping the system current in the Troubleshooting Guide for HPE ProLiant Gen10 servers at http://www.hpe.com/info/Gen10- troubleshooting. To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
