    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Make sure there is enough power supply to distribute power. Go to, the Chassis Overview &gt; Power &gt; Power Budget Status. In the Total Input Power Available For Allocation field, view the available power. To add more power, insert more PSUs or remove unused components from the chassis.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0371/procedure/01/item/024">
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the DIMM. CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system board connector. See the DIMM handling guidelines on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Library at: http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs</diag:itemText>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
