  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N7c60c2f2dc1044919f90e97c7fa3bf54">
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-TMP1000/procedure/01"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-TMP1000/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-TMP1000"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Check for factors that may cause overheating. For example, verify that the enclosure fan is working. You should check the thermostat settings and examine whether the enclosure is located near a heat source. Make sure the enclosure has enough ventilation and that the room temperature is not too hot. Refer to the enclosure documentation for more diagnostic information.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
