    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: If the controller is a PCIe card, verify that the controller backup power cable is installed properly.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0369/message/01">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0369 message 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#MessageTemplate"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:messageText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A POST message displays: System ROM authentication error – The system is operating on a recovered or redundant image. Redundant ROM functionality is NOT available.</diag:messageText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Nc6a7e3d0b81f4861bfe6b76fa993ff7b">
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PSU0051"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PSU0051/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/DELL-EEM-2026-EEM-PSU0051/procedure/01"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Ensure that Chassis Zone-1 has at least one PSU installed. If there is already a PSU installed in Zone-1, remove and re-insert it. Ensure that the LED status is green. It the issue persists, Collect a SupportAssist collection (TSR) report using iDRAC. Visit https://www.dell.com/support/incidents- online/contactus/dynamic to use the Virtual Assistant to analyze the collection and recommend a resolution.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0410/procedure/01/item/013">
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">13</diag:itemOrder>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [1205, 2470); FULL_TEXT_SOURCE_MARKERS; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: SOURCE_ANCHORED_RULE_LINK. Explicit action verb and shared documented component/condition in the same source group; inferred intended purpose only.</rdfs:comment>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Run SUT from the command line (On-Demand mode) to update the Smart Array firmware. For more information, see to the HP SUT documents at http://www.hpe.com/info/sut-docs. Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP): Update the Smart Array firmware by downloading the SPP from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Refer to the SPP documentation at http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/ documentation for instructions on updating the firmware. Note: Downloading an SPP requires a contract with Hewlett Packard Enterprise and an HPE Passport ID. If you do not have an HPE Passport ID, go to http://www.hpe.com/info/insightonline. Note: Downloading the entire SPP can take a significant amount of time. Online Flash components This component provides updated system firmware that can be installed directly on supported operating systems. Additionally, when used in conjunction with the SUM, this Smart Component allows you to update firmware on remote servers from a central location. This remote deployment capability eliminates the need for you to be physically present at the server to perform a firmware update. For specific instructions on updating firmware, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide, at http:// www.hpe.com/info/hpsum/documentation.</diag:itemText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0410 printed item 13</rdfs:label>
    <diag:sourceLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3.</diag:sourceLabel>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <diag:addressesCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x0410/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
