  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01/item/008"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Security%20module"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-318/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 318 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  Reboot the server.
2.  When a TPM is installed and is being used with BitLocker, be sure that the TPM is enabled in UEFI
System Utilities.
For more information, see the following:
•  The UEFI System Utilities user guide for your product on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website
(https://www.hpe.com/info/uefi/docs).
•  The TPM replacement recovery procedure in the operating system documentation.
3.  Be sure that the TPM is configured for a mode that is compatible with the OS running on the server.
4.  Verify that the OS supports the version of TPM installed and configured on the server.
5.  When a TPM 2.0 is installed, verify that the server is configured for UEFI boot mode:
From the System Utilities screen, select System Configuration &gt; BIOS/Platform Configuration
(RBSU) &gt; Boot Options &gt; Boot Mode.
6.  If the issue persists, open a support case using the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Support Center
website (https://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc).</diag:procedureText>
  </rdf:Description>
