    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Cooling%20device"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: System detected repeated thermal trips due to excessive heat. Check for obstructions to the fan and vents. Make sure BIOS is current and rerun diagnostics. If error persists replace thermal heat sink, CPU and motherboard.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0209/procedure/01">
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0209/procedure/01/item/006"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0209/procedure/01/item/002"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0209/procedure/01/item/004"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0209/procedure/01/item/003"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0209/procedure/01/item/007"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0209/procedure/01/item/005"/>
    <diag:hasItem rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0209/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <diag:considersCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x0209/procedure/01/cause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0209 recommendation 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#RecoveryProcedure"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:procedureText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Install the DIMMs in a supported configuration.
CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system board
connector.
To reseat the memory
1.  Power down the server.
2.  Remove all power:
a.  Disconnect each power cord from the power source.
b.  Disconnect each power cord from the server.
For additional information, see the server maintenance and sever guide located at http://
www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs.
If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.
1.  Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the:
Customer Self Repair website.
This enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For
specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service
guide.
2.  Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc.
HPE Support will contact you.</diag:procedureText>
    <diag:targetsComponentType rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Memory%20module"/>
