  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-POST-378/procedure/01/cause">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#PossibleCause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:causeText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The server does not match the original server in which the NVDIMM was used, and NVDIMM-N Memory
Interleaving is enabled.
CAUTION:
Before removing or replacing any processors, be sure to follow the guidelines
in "Processor troubleshooting guidelines" in the troubleshooting guide for your
product. Failure to follow the recommended guidelines can cause damage to the
system board, requiring replacement of the system board.</diag:causeText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 378 possible cause 1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-GEN9-V2-Virtual-Connect-3023/procedure/01/cause">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#PossibleCause"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 3023 possible cause 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:causeText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">•  Configuration of IP addresses/network topology is preventing communication between the primary
VC-Enet module and the identified VC-Enet module.
•  An unexpected error has occurred while sending a configuration update to the module or while
requesting status information from the module. This error may be due to TCP/IP communications
interruption/timeout or due to a software generated failure.
•  The primary VC-Enet module is unable to exchange network packets with the indicated module. This
inability can occur if the Onboard Administrator has configured the internal switch that connects the I/O
modules inappropriately.</diag:causeText>
  </rdf:Description>
