  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0005-0x0005/procedure/01/item/001">
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">1</diag:itemOrder>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reseat the processor. WARNING: To reduce the risk of personal injury from hot surfaces, allow the drives and the internal system components to cool before touching them. CAUTION: THE PINS ON THE SYSTEM BOARD ARE VERY FRAGILE AND EASILY DAMAGED. To avoid damage to the system board, do not touch the processor or the processor socket contacts. Important: Only authorized technicians trained by Hewlett Packard Enterprise should attempt to remove or replace a processor. If you believe the processor requires replacement, contact Hewlett Packard Enterprise technical support before proceeding. Create a Hewlett Packard Enterprise Support Case.</diag:itemText>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: SOURCE_ANCHORED_RULE_LINK. Explicit action verb and shared documented component/condition in the same source group; inferred intended purpose only.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 642); ACTIONABLE_SOURCE_PREFIX; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0005 printed item 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <diag:addressesCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0005-0x0005/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
