  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000B-0x0028/procedure/01/cause">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x0028 possible cause 1</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#PossibleCause"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <diag:causeText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.  The power supply might not be fully seated.
2.  AC power is unavailable.
3.  The power supply failed.
4.  The power supply is in standby mode.
5.  The power supply has exceeded the current limit.
6.  The power supply is not supported on the server.
7.  The power is not sufficient for the hardware installed.
8.  Redundant power supplies are configured but the power supplies are not compatible.</diag:causeText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Nc3024788d4b446a0953be7680254ef7b">
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1921"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1921/procedure/01/item/001"/>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x000A-0x1921/procedure/01"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Enclosure%20or%20backplane"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Upgrade the enclosure firmware and the controller firmware. Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation). To update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components. To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs. If the issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
