    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#targetsComponentType"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Run SUT from the command line (On-Demand mode) to update the Smart Array firmware. For more information, see to the HP SUT documents at http://www.hpe.com/info/sut-docs. Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP): Update the Smart Array firmware by downloading the SPP from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Refer to the SPP documentation at http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/ documentation for instructions on updating the firmware. Note: Downloading an SPP requires a contract with Hewlett Packard Enterprise and an HPE Passport ID. If you do not have an HPE Passport ID, go to http://www.hpe.com/info/insightonline. Note: Downloading the entire SPP can take a significant amount of time.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
