  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x3025/procedure/01/item/001">
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 1251); UNNUMBERED_SOURCE_BLOCK; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: SOURCE_ANCHORED_RULE_LINK. Explicit action verb and shared documented component/condition in the same source group; inferred intended purpose only.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting#ProcedureItem"/>
    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Remove the Intel Optane PMem for HPE Modules with unsupported model types. If the hardware levels of all PMEMs are the same, there may be different levels of firmware running on the PMEM controllers. Upgrade the firmware version of the PMEMs to the same level. This may require booting with individual PMEMs installed during the process To update firmware:. Service Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation). To update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components. To update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the HPE Synergy Firmware Update Overview at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.</diag:itemText>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x3025 printed item 1</rdfs:label>
    <diag:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger">1</diag:itemOrder>
    <diag:nestingLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</diag:nestingLevel>
    <diag:addressesCause rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/event/HPE-IML-2026-IML-Class-0x0032-0x3025/procedure/01/cause"/>
  </rdf:Description>
