    <diag:itemText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Install memory. Consult the User Guide for more information on supported configurations. For DIMM population, see the Population rules for HPE DDR4 memory with HPE ProLiant and Synergy Gen10 servers (http://www.hpe.com/docs/memory-population-rules) CAUTION: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system board connector. See the Best Practices for Handling Memory Modules in ProLiant Server Configurations (http://h20564.www2.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docId=emr_na-c00868283). If this issue persists, create an HPE Support Case.</diag:itemText>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Source action_text character span [0, 573); ACTIONABLE_SOURCE_PREFIX; order is printed/text order, not an execution dependency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Purpose assessment: AMBIGUOUS_CORRESPONDENCE. An action exists, but its target cannot be tied to the documented cause by the conservative rules.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HPE 0x3016 printed item 1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
