    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://example.org/server-troubleshooting/data/component-type/Processor"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Automatic source-text assessment: explicit diagnostic/corrective verb and component mention in the instruction. This is a procedure target, not necessarily the component responsible for the event. Evidence: Reseat the processor WARNING: To reduce the risk of personal injury from hot surfaces, allow the drives and the internal system components to cool before touching them. CAUTION: THE PINS ON THE SYSTEM BOARD ARE VERY FRAGILE AND EASILY DAMAGED. To avoid damage to the system board, do not touch the processor or the processor socket contacts. IMPORTANT: Both processor sockets must always be populated. If either processor socket is empty, the server does not power up. Reseat the memory</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
